course: dictionary
lesson: 8697
title: Sell and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word sell is a verb, and its forms are sell, sells, sold and selling. To sell something means to give it to someone in return for money. A shop sells bread, and you pay for it.
explain: Sell can also mean that something is bought by people. «The book sells well» does not mean the book is being given away. It means many people are buying it. Look at the words around sell to find out which meaning fits.
explain: Sometimes sell means making people like an idea or agree with it. If someone wants to sell her plan to the class, she wants them to think the plan is good. Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: «Sell» means to give something to someone in return for money.
fact: «Sold» is the past form, as in «The shopkeeper sold the bread yesterday.»
fact: «Sell out» means to sell all of something, so none is left.
fact: «For sale» and «on sale» both mean that something can be bought.
exercise: «A shop sells only whole loaves.» What does sells mean here? | Hides from customers | Makes them in a kitchen | *Gives to customers in return for money | Throws them away
exercise: «The book sells well.» What does this mean? | The book is very loud | *Many people buy the book | The book is written in pencil | The book is hidden on a shelf
exercise: What is the past form of sell? | *Sold | Sells | Seller | Selling
test: «Before a new medicine is sold, it is tested on many volunteers.» What does sold mean here? | *Given to people for money, once it is safe | Hidden in a box | Given away free to friends | Thrown away
test: Mia says, «She wants to sell her plan to the whole class.» What does sell mean here? | Give the plan away for no money | *Make people like the plan and agree with it | Lose the plan | Copy the plan onto paper
exam: «Codes and currency sold cheaply by strangers are often fake.» Why should you be careful? | *Such things are often stolen or fake, so only official shops are safe | Codes are not worth reading | Strangers always sell good things | Cheap things are always the best
